<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Mayne chairman Webber says to retire.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Mayne chairman Webber says to retire.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mayne Nickless Ltd Chairman Ian Webber said on Tuesday he planned to retire and that director Mark Raynor would succeed him as chairman in 1997.  </p>
<p>&quot;Now that the company has embarked on this direction I have concluded, somewhat reluctantly, that it is the right time for me to step down after five years as chairman, and 10 years as managing director,&quot; Webber told Mayne's annual general meeting.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
